.TH mouser-mcp 1  "mouser-mcp 1.4.4" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-mcp \- Mouser\*(Aqs MCP server (tabs, screen, shell, files for MCP clients); see docs/mcp.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser mcp\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mouser\*(Aqs MCP server (tabs, screen, shell, files for MCP clients); see docs/mcp.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-serve(1)
Speak MCP on stdin/stdout, bridged to the running Mouser (for clients that start servers)
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-status(1)
Show whether it\*(Aqs on, the endpoints, the certificate and where the token is
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-enable(1)
Turn the server on (loopback HTTP; `\-\-https` adds TLS with a self\-signed or your cert)
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-disable(1)
Turn it off
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-cert(1)
The HTTPS certificate: `status`, or `renew` a Let\*(Aqs Encrypt one now
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-token(1)
Print (`\-\-show`) or replace (`\-\-rotate`) the bearer token
.TP
mouser\-mcp\-servers(1)
MCP servers Mouser connects to (`[[mcp.servers]]`; tools in the sidebar)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
